  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5200",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to be a potential modulator of SNU-16 through a series of molecular interactions involving palmarumycin CP18. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N directly targets A704, Ubiquitin carboxyl-terminal hydrolase 5, and P2X purinoceptor 1, all of which are subsequently targeted by palmarumycin CP18. This creates a cascade of molecular effects that ultimately lead to the inhibition of SNU-16. The scores from the three paths indicate a consistent level of confidence in this relationship, with the highest score (0.5856) supporting the direct interaction between Mollicellin N and SNU-16 through the palmarumycin CP18 pathway. The presence of multiple independent pathways converging on SNU-16 suggests a robust mechanism of action, potentially involving the regulation of cellular processes through the modulation of these receptors and enzymes. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the molecular interactions and underscores the importance of understanding the specific mechanisms by which Mollicellin N exerts its effects on SNU-16.",
